\details{
The two frames tell the same story with one difference worth showing: for
eggs the gap between the two areas is roughly constant through the season,
while for adult females it is not. The ratio runs at about two at either end
of the season and widens to nearly four in August, which is why the
published model for this response carries a day-by-area interaction that the
egg model does not.
}
